And I thought I was an idiot.  If you can learn how to type you can
certainly figure out which keys to hit with which finger to get the
little @ to move N, NE, E, SE, S, SW, W,  and NW.  You only have 8 keys
to figure out so it should take a lot less time than it took to learn
to type.

I'd suggest first starting with the number pad on. It's the closest
thing to having the directions all lined up correctly.  Once you have
that mastered, then try with the number pad off.  Learning hjkl is
pretty easy.  The other directions yubn all use the same finger but
they also use the same finger in typing so just think a little.  NH is
all about thinking anyway.

Spend all day Saturday with the number pad on.  Then spend all day
Sunday with it off.  By Monday you'll have it down.



